RULE NUMBER
007

TITLE
Forge: Component README (component-root README.md)

ROLE
You are the Planton Code Partner working inside the developer's local workspace in Cursor. This rule runs after proto files exist and generates the component's `README.md` -- the GitHub-facing component page at the COMPONENT ROOT (`catalog/<provider>/<kindfolder>/README.md`), beside `catalog.md` and `logo.svg`, never inside the version directory.

TOOLS
- Proto Readers: reuse `_rules/component/_scripts/*_reader.py` for `api.proto`, `spec.proto`, `input.proto`, `outputs.proto` as needed.
- Docs Writer: `_rules/component/_scripts/readme_write.py` writes the component-root `README.md` deterministically.
  The writer guarantees the README ends with the canonical license footer (the attribution
  that travels with a copied component; enforced in CI by lint.license-footers) — drafts may
  include it or omit it, the tool ensures exactly one.
- Reference components (live ground truth): `catalog/aws/awsvpc/README.md`
  and `catalog/aws/awsalb/README.md` -- canonical user-facing README structure and tone.

SCOPE
- Target: `catalog/<provider>/<kindfolder>/README.md` (the component root).
- Create/update `README.md`.

SEQUENTIAL STEPS
1) Read: Use proto readers to fetch contents of `api.proto`, `spec.proto`, `input.proto`, `outputs.proto`.
2) Draft: Generate README content using proto details, modeled on the reference component `README.md` files.
3) Write: `python3 _rules/component/_scripts/readme_write.py --provider <provider> --kindfolder <kindfolder> --readme-file <path>`
   - If edits are needed, refine content and re-run (≤3).

SUCCESS CRITERIA
 - `README.md` exists at the component root
 - Docs list fields and outputs accurately and reference official docs

OUTPUT STYLE IN CHAT
- Show created/updated paths and brief outline of sections.
- Show the deterministic tool invocation and key outputs.

NOTES
- Keep docs concise and practical. Record official URLs and brief rationale for field choices.
